    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0928" n="846" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg846"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Motley</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 185.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 8th instant, No. 170, which paper is accompanied by a
                    copy of a note which, on the 6th instant, you addressed to Count Mensdorff in
                    execution of my instructions Nos. 173, 174, and 176.</p>
                <p>I have great pleasure in saying that the President approves entirely of the
                    proceedings on your part which are related in your despatch, and equally
                    approves of your note to the Austrian minister for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Lothrop Motley</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Vienna</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
